# Resizing: the screen reflows, the cursor stays on its text.
#
# xterm itself does not reflow (it cuts and pads lines); this engine does, so these cases are
# conventions of the engine rather than of a published text. They pin down what must stay true: the text, its order and where the cursor is.

test widening joins a wrapped row
convention rows that were wrapped by autowrap are one line again when the screen is wide enough
size 5 4
feed abcdefgh
resize 10 4
screen
|abcdefgh|
cursor 1,9
wrapped 1 no

test narrowing keeps the text of a long row
convention a line longer than the new width wraps onto further rows; the text and its order do not change
size 10 4
feed abcdefghijkl
resize 5 4
lines
|abcdefghijkl|
cursor *,3

test narrowing keeps the rows on screen when they fit
convention rows that still fit the screen after reflow stay on it; they are not pushed into the history
known-fail: alacritty – reflow keeps the cursor on its screen row and pushes the rows above it into the history even when everything fits
size 10 4
feed abcdefghijkl
resize 5 4
screen
|abcde|
|fghij|
|kl|
cursor 3,3
wrapped 1 yes
wrapped 2 yes
wrapped 3 no
scrollback-len 0

test widening keeps rows that ended with a line break apart
convention only autowrapped rows are joined
size 5 4
feed ab\r\ncd
resize 10 4
lines
|ab|
|cd|
screen
|ab|
|cd|

test narrowing and widening again restores the line
convention reflow is lossless for plain text
size 10 4
feed abcdefghijkl
resize 5 4
resize 10 4
lines
|abcdefghijkl|
cursor *,3

test growing the height adds blank rows below
convention with no history the new rows are blank and the content stays where it was
size 10 2
feed A\r\nB
resize 10 4
screen
|A|
|B|
cursor 2,2

test shrinking the height keeps the cursor row on screen
convention lines above the cursor move into the history so that the cursor row stays visible
size 10 4
feed A\r\nB\r\nC\r\nD
resize 10 2
screen
|C|
|D|
cursor 2,2
scrollback
|A|
|B|

test the cursor stays inside after narrowing
convention the cursor is clamped to the new size
size 10 4
feed \e[1;10H
resize 5 4
cursor 1,5

test resizing keeps the rendition of the text
convention reflow keeps the cell attributes with the text
size 5 4
feed \e[31mabcdefg
resize 10 4
cell 1,7 text=g fg=idx:1
cell 1,1 text=a fg=idx:1

test resizing does not leave the alternate screen
convention resize is not a mode change
size 10 4
feed \e[?1049h
resize 6 3
alt-screen on
feed \e[?1049l
alt-screen off

test resizing resets the scrolling region
convention a resize returns the margins to the whole screen, as DECSLPP/DECSCPP do
size 10 4
feed \e[2;3r
resize 10 6
feed \e[6;1H\n
scrollback-len 1

test wide characters are not split by narrowing
convention a wide character that does not fit at the end of a row moves to the next one whole
size 6 4
feed ab日cd
resize 3 4
lines
|ab日cd|

test resize on the alternate screen leaves it without history
spec xterm ctlseqs: the alternate screen buffer has no scrollback (CSI ? 1049 h)
size 5 3
feed \e[?1049h
resize 5 4
feed 1\n2\n3\n4\n5\n6\n
scrollback-len 0
